  "formal_boundary": "The all-clock correction inequality, arbitrary-block valuation loss, and finite Q*2^h actual-return threshold are Lean theorems. The external published S-unit theorem, its sparse-endpoint specialization and density deduction remain written mathematics. Canonical BV, sector computations, subcritical forcing, and terminal energy commutator are written deductions retaining the pinned analytic assumptions. No deep theorem is imported as a custom axiom.",
